    "ls|LS17_S11_U_1": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 1\n(To be answered on the 2nd February 2023)\n \nEXPANSION OF AIRPORT\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to expand the airport network and take\nair travel to the smallest cities in the country;\n(b) if so, the details thereof; and\n(c) if not, the reasons therefor?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a) to (c): Ministry of Civil Aviation has launched Regional Connectivity\nScheme (RCS) - UDAN (Ude Desh ka Aam Nagrik) on 21.10.2016 to stimulate\nregional air connectivity and making air travel affordable to the masses. An\nairport which is included in the awarded routes of UDAN and requires\nupgradation / development for commencement of flight operations, is\ndeveloped under \"Revival/upgradation of unserved and underserved\nairports/heliports/water aerodromes\" Scheme.\n \nAs on 20.01.2023, after four rounds of bidding under UDAN, 459 routes have\ncommenced, operationalizing 72 Airports including 2 Water Aerodrome & 9\nHeliports. More than 2.16 lakh UDAN flights have been operated and over\n1.13 crore passengers have availed the benefits in UDAN flights so far. The\nscheme has been able to provide air connectivity to Tier-2 &Tier-3 cities\nacross the country at affordable airfares and has transformed the way people\ntravel.\n \n \n \n*****\n1. SHRI S. JAGATHRAKSHAKAN\n be pleased to state:-\n (GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD))",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_10": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 10\n(To be answered on the 2nd February 2023)\n \nFLIGHT DISRUPTIONS DUE TO FOG\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) whether the movement of aircraft were widely affected and the passengers had to face\na lot of difficulties due to low visibility at Darbhanga airport during winter and if so, the\ndetails thereof;\n(b) whether installation of Clear Air Turbulence (CAT-2 ILS) and Aeronautical Ground\nLighting System (AGLS) is underway since 2021 to address the said problem but the said\nwork is not completed till now and if so, the details thereof;\n(c) the time by which the above works are likely to be completed; and\n(d) the details of the action plan of the Government for development of the said airport?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n*****\n*10. SHRI GOPAL JEE THAKUR\n be pleased to state:-\n (Shri Jyotiraditya M. Scindia)\n\nStatement in reply to parts (a) to (d) of the Starred (*) Question No. 10 for answer on\n02.02.2023 regarding 'Flight Disruptions due to Fog'.\n \n(a): During the  Winter Schedule of 2022-23 (from 01.12.2022 to 29.01.2023), 64 aircraft\nmovements (Arrival & Departure) got cancelled at Darbhanga airport, due to low\nvisibility conditions.\n \n(b) & (c): Darbhanga Airport is owned and operated by Indian Air Force (IAF) and\nAirports Authority of India (AAI) maintains a Civil Enclave. IAF is responsible for\nmaintenance/ upgradation of airside infrastructure. As informed by IAF, works are in\nprogress for installation of Category II (CAT II) Instrument Landing System (ILS) with\nAeronautical Ground Lighting System (AGLS) as part of Modernization of Airfield\nProject with the probable date of completion as April 2024.\n \n(d): Airports Authority of India (AAI) has taken up strengthening of Runway, taxi track,\napron and construction of runway shoulders, Runway End Safety Area (RESA) and Blast\nPad at Darbhanga airport. \n*****",
