    "ls|LS17_S11_U_50": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 50\n(To be answered on the 2nd February 2023)\n \nPARTNERSHIP OF AAI WITH CIDC\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) whether the Airports Authority of India (AAI) in collaboration with\nConstruction Industry Development Council (CIDC) has trained youth in the\naviation sector and if so, the details thereof along with the number of people\nwho got trained during the last three years;\n(b) if not, the reasons therefor;\n(c) the number of commercial pilot licences issued by the Directorate General\nof Civil Aviation (DGCA) to the trainees who got trained by various institutes\nin the country during the last three years; and\n(d) the number of pilot who got employment out of the said license-holders?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a) and (b) Airports Authority of India (AAI) in collaboration with\nConstruction Industry Development Council (CIDC) provided job oriented\nskill training and employment opportunities through livelihood promotion in\nbackward and remote areas. The details are as under:-\n \nProgram                                                        No. of Trained\n \nEmployment Oriented                                         1999\nTraining & Skill Development\nprogramme of unemployed\nyouth SC/ST/OBC Women and\nEWS of Society for 2000 persons\nby CIDC (PAN India).\nFY 2018-19 (CIDC).\n \n \n50. SHRI SHANKAR LALWANI\n be pleased to state:-\n (GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD))\n\nEmployment Oriented Training                          1604\nand Skill Development Programme\nfor SC/ST/OBC/ Women, Unemployed\nYouth & EWS Society for 2000\nPersons North Eastern Region\nFY 2018-19 (CIDC).\n \n(c) The total number of Commercial Pilot Licenses (CPL) issued by the\nDirectorate General of Civil Aviation (DGCA) during the last three years is as\nunder\n \nYear    CPL issued to     CPL issued to      Total\n           cadets from         cadets from              \n           Indian Institute    Foreign Institute\n                     \n \n2020              335                243                  578\n2021              504                358                  862\n2022              616                549                 1165\nTotal            1455              1150                 2605\n \n(d) DGCA issues licenses as per the provisions and on compliance of Aircraft\nRules 1937. Post issue of licenses, license holders can undetake employment in\nany International Civil Aviation Organisation (ICAO) contracting state.\n \n*****",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_51": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 51 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.02.2023 \n \nTribal Universities \n \n†*51. SHRIMATI GEETA KORA: \n SHRI B.B. PATIL: \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the number of tribal students who go outside the tribal dominated areas to get education; \n \n(b) the number of Central Tribal Universities in the country along with the tribal students \nstudying therein, State-wise; \n \n(c) whether the Government proposes to set  up Tribal Universities in the country including \nBihar, Jharkhand, Gujarat, Madhya Pradesh and Telangana, if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d) whether the Union Government has received  proposals from State Governments in this \nregard and if so, the details thereof along with the action taken thereon; and \n \n(e) the standard prescribed to open Central Tribal University? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (e):  A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n***** \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a ) TO ( e) OF  LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.  51 FOR ANSWER ON 06.02.2023 REGARDING TRIBAL \nUNIVERSITIES ASKED BY SHRIMATI GEETA KORA, HON’BLE MP AND SHRI B.B \nPATIL, HON’BLE MP \n \n(a): As per All India Survey on Higher Education  (AISHE), 2020-21, 24.10 lakh tribal \nstudents have enrolled in the Higher education Institutions in the country. \n \n(b) to (e): There are  two Ce ntral Tribal Universities in the country namely Indira Gandhi \nNational Tribal University (IGNTU) , Amarkantak , Madhya Pradesh and Central Tribal \nUniversity of Andhra Pradesh (CTUAP) , Vizianagram, Andhra Pradesh wherein 523 tribal \nstudents are studying.  Setting up of a Central University is a continuous process and is setup as \nand when need arises. There is no prescribed standard for setting up such university.  The Union \nGovernment has not received any proposal from State Governments in this regard.  However, as \nper Andhra Pradesh Reorganisation Act, 2014, there is a provision for setting up of a Central \nTribal University in the State of Telangana. \n \n*** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_52": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*52  \nANSWERED ON 06.02.2023 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF SABARIMALA \n \n*52.  SHRI KUMBAKUDI SUDHAKARAN: \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether it is true that Rs.80 crore out of a total of Rs.100 crore \nthat was allotted by the Union Government for the development \nof Sabarimala under Swadesh Darshan Scheme lapsed on \nDecember 31,2022; \n(b)  if so, the reasons leading to this situation along with the details \nof the master plan submitted by the State Government on \nSabarimala and if not, the reasons therefor; \n(c)  the steps taken by the Government to direct the State \nauthorities for the utilisation of the fund before the stipulated \ndeadline; \n(d)  whether the Government is aware that the projects costing \nRs.20 crore as per the master plan of Sabarimala have not been \ncompleted yet; and \n(e)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n  \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF TOURISM          (SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n******* \n\n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO.*52 ANSWERED ON 06.02.2023 REGARDING \nDEVELOPMENT OF SABARIMALA. \n \n(a) to (e): The Ministry of Tourism has sanctioned a project \n‘Development of Sabarimala – Erumeli – Pampa – Sannidhanam’ in \n2016-17 for an amount of Rs.99.99 Cr. The completion date of this \nproject was December, 2022. In addition, the Ministry of Tourism also \nsanctioned a project ‘Development of Sree Padmanabha- Aranmula- \nSabrimala in 2016-17 for Rs.92.44 Cr., which also included \ndevelopment work at Sabarimala. The development work of Rs. 6.10 \nCrore (plus contingency/consultancy) sanctioned at Sabarimala site \nwas dropped from the second project and added to the first project i.e. \n‘Development of Sabarimala – Erumeli – Pampa – Sannidhanam’, thus \nelevating the sanctioned cost of this project to Rs.106.42 Cr.  \n \n ‘Development of Sabarimala – Erumeli – Pampa – Sannidhanam’ \nproject was reviewed by the Ministry of Tourism in August, 2022 and \nthe Ministry of Tourism noted no progress in respect of the \ncomponents for Rs.49.10 Crore and thereafter on the request of the \nState Government, the said project was revised in October, 2022 to \nRs.54.88 Crore. Details of the project sanctioned for Rs.106.41 Crore \nand later revised to Rs. 54.88 Crore is tabulated as under:-  \n \nDestination Sanctioned \namount \n(Rs. in Crore) \nRevised sanction \namount  \n(Rs. in Crore) \nSabrimala Temple – Erumeli 2.8 2.8 \nPampa 32.97 11.07 \nTrekking Path 26.56 20.23 \nSannidham 32.90 16.01 \nSabrimala (transferred from \nPadmanabha Project) \n6.12 2.16 \nContingency  3.04 1.57 \nConsultancy  2.02 1.04 \nTotal 106.41 54.88 \n \n\n \n \nTimely completion of the sanctioned project and implementation of \nmaster plan is the responsibility of the State Government. However, \nthe Ministry of Tourism regular monitors the progress of the projects \nto ensure its speedy completion. There is a recorded physical \nprogress of 75% in respect of revised ‘Development of Sabarimala – \nErumeli – Pampa – Sannidhanam’ project.  \n \n*******  ",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_53": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION No. 53 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.02.2023 \n \nGuidelines for Crematoriums \n \n \n*53.  DR. RAMAPATI RAM TRIPATHI: \nSHRI SANGAM LAL GUPTA: \n \nWill the Minister of ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether the Government acknowledges that the crematoriums are also a major \ncontributor to Air Pollution; \n(b) if so, the action taken to mitigate it and if not, the reasons therefor; \n \n(c) whether the Government is planning to develop any enforceable standards or guidelines \nfor crematoriums, specifically for those in urban areas; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER FOR ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE  \n(SHRI BHUPENDER YADAV) \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n  \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARAS (a) TO (d) OF THE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 53 DUE FOR REPLY ON 06.02.2023 \nREGARDING ‘GUIDELINES FOR CREMATORIUMS’ RAISED BY DR. \nRAMAPATI RAM TRIPATHI AND SHRI SANGAM LAL GUPTA, HON’BLE \nMEMBERS OF PARLIAMENT \n \n \n(a) to (d) \n \n \nAs per the available Source Apportionment study reports from 2018 to 2022, no such \ncontribution in air pollution is observed from crematoriums.  \n \nThe development of guidelines on environment management for crematoria has been taken up \nby Central Pollution Control Board. This includes inventory and in-depth study in selective \ncrematorium at different cities of the country.The activities taken under in-depth study \ninclude: identification of source of emissions, monitoring of fugitive as well as source \nemission to assess the level of concentrations, comparison of various technologies in terms of \nfuel consumption, time for cremation, environmental benefits, cost analysis of various \ntechnologies and assessment of the appropriateness of pollution control devices. \n \n****** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_54": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.†*54 \nANSWERED ON 06.02.2023 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF RELIGIOUS PLACES UNDER PRASAD \nSCHEME \n \n†*54. SHRI NAYAB SINGH: \n  \n Will the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has covered various tourist places of \nHaryana under the PRASAD scheme; \n(b) if so, the district-wise details thereof; \n(c) whether the Government is making any  special provision for \nreligious places like Mata Mansa Devi Mandir, Nada Sahib \nlocated in Panch kula and Adi Badri in Haryana through the \nsaid scheme so that the devotees visiting the said places may \nget the benefit of the said scheme as well as to develop the \nsaid places with ultra modern facilities; \n(d) whether the Government is likely to include n ew components \nin the PRASAD scheme which may also benefit the rural areas; \nand \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF TOURISM          (SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n(a) to (e) : A Statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n \n**** \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO .†*54 ANSWERED ON 06.02.2023 \nREGARDING DEVELOPMENT OF RELIGIOUS PLACES UNDER \nPRASAD SCHEME. \n \n \n(a) to  (c): Under PRASHAD Scheme of Ministry of Tourism, \ndestinations are identified and projects are approved on the basis of \nproposal requests received from the respective State \nGovernments/Union Territory Administrations. Based on the \nproposals received from Sta te Government of Haryana , Nada Saheb \nGurudwara and Mata Mansha Devi Temple in Panchkula di strict \nhave been included under PRASHAD scheme. A Project viz. \n“Development of Nada Saheb Gurudwara and Mata Mansha Devi \nTemple in Panchkula District”  at the estimated  cost of Rs. 49.52 Cr. \nhas been approved under the scheme for development of pilgrimage \ntourism amenities at these destinations. \n \n(d) & (e): PRASHAD is a  scheme for development of Pilgrimage and \nHeritage tourism infrastructure at the identified destination s across \nthe country irrespective the location of identified destination , \nwhether it falls under rural, urban, tribal or in any other area and the \nbenefits of the projects are available to the local population. \n  \n******** ",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_55": "������������������� �\n��������������������� �\n������������������������������ �\n�\n��������� �\n� ������������������ �����\n����������� �������������\n�\n������������ ���������������������������������\n�������������������������� �\n�\n�\n��������������������������������� �\n�����������������������������������������������������\n�\n���� �������� ���� ����������� ��� ���� ������� ������ ��� ������������� ��������� ��� �����\n����������� ��������������������������� ����� �������� ��������� ������������ ����� ���� ��������\n��������� ��������� ������������ ��������� ���������� ������������ ��������� ���� ������ ��������\n�����������������������������\n���������������������������������\n���� ������������ ������� ������ ��� ���� ������ ������������ ������� ����� ������������� ��������� ���\n����������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������ �\n���� ������������ ���������� �\n������������������������ ��\n����������� �����������������������������������������������\n�\n������\n� �\n\n���������� ��������� ��� ��� ������ ��� ������ ���� ��� ���� ��� ���� ������\n����� ��� ��������� ���� ��� ���� ����������� ������ ��� ����� ������� ������\n����� ���� ���������������� �������������� ������ ���������������������� ���������������������� ���� ���\n��� ����������������������������������������������������������� �\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������� ��������� ����������� ������������� ������������� ������������� ���� �����������\n��� ���������� ��������� ��� ����������������� ������������ ����� ���� �������� ��������� ��