    "ls|LS17_S11_U_9": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \nLOK SABHA  \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 9 \nANSWERED ON 02.02.2023 \n \nIMPLEMENTATION OF PM-KUSUM \n \n*9. SHRI VISHNU DATT SHARMA \n \nWill the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether Pradhan Mantri Kisan Urja Evam Utthaan Mahabhiyan (PM-KUSUM) scheme is \nbeing implemented in the State of Madhya Pradesh; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) the details of the installations of decentralised ground mounted grid connected renewable \npower plants, standalone solar powered agriculture pumps and solarisation of grid connected \nagriculture pumps supported so far under components A, B & C of the scheme across Madhya \nPradesh, especially in the districts of Panna, Katni and Chhatarpur?  \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND POWER  \n \n(SHRI R.K. SINGH)  \n \n(a) to (c) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n***** \n  \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT \n \nStatement referred to in reply to parts (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. 9 to be \nanswered on 02.02.2023 regarding Implementation of PM-KUSUM \n \n(a)to (c) The Pradhan Mantri Kisan Urja Evam Utthaan Mahabhiyan (PM -KUSUM) is a demand \ndriven Scheme and open for all States/UTs, including the State of Madhya Pradesh, for \nparticipation in the Scheme. The Scheme consists of following three components: \n \n• Component-A: installation of aggregated 10,000 MW capacity of small solar power plants, \neach of capacity upto 2 MW on the barren/fallow/pasture/marshy land of farmers. Further, \nthese plants can also be installed on cultivable lands on stilt allowing genera tion of solar \npower and cultivation simultaneously. \n• Component-B: installation of 20 lakh standalone solar water pumps; and \n• Component-C: solarization of 15 lakh existing grid-connected agriculture pumps including \nthrough feeder level solarisation. \n \nBased on the demand received from the State of Madhya Pradesh, capacities were allocated under \nthe three components of the Scheme. The capacities allocated and installations reported under the \nthree components of the Scheme in the state of Madhya Pradesh are as under: \nComponent Sanctioned Capacity/ Quantity Installed Capacity/ Quantity \nComponent-A 500 MW 4 MW \nComponent-B  12,000 nos. 6787 nos. \nComponent-C 2,70,000 nos.  0 \n \nUnder Component-B of the PM -KUSUM Scheme, 39 standalone solar pumps in district Panna, \n150 nos. pumps in district Katni, and 66 nos. pumps in district Chhatarpur have been reported \ninstalled. No installations have been reported so far in the said districts  under Component-A and \nComponent-C of the Scheme.  \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S11_U_90": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 90 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 08.02.2023 \n \nRESTORATION OF TRAINS \n \n†*90. SHRI MAHABALI SINGH: \n      \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the names of trains which were discontinued in 2020 before the \nonset of COVID -19 pandemic and those trains that have resumed \noperations; \n \n(b) the names of those trains in which linen and catering services \nhave not been restored so far; and \n \n(c) the names of the trains which have not restarted their operations \nso far, division-wise? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW)  \n \n(a) to (c)  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 90 BY SHRI MAHABALI SINGH  TO BE ANSWERED IN \nLOK SABHA ON 08.02.2023 REGARDING RESTORATION OF TRAINS \n \n(a) to  (c) Indian Railways, to contain the spread of COVID-19 pandemic, \nhad discontinued all regular passengers carrying trains, including \nMail/Express trains, w.e.f 23.03.2020 and only special trains with \nlimited stoppages were being operated. Further, India n Railways have \nundertaken rationalization of the time table, including rationalization of \ntrain services, in a scientific manner with the assistance of IIT-Bombay. \nThe exercise has been undertaken inter alia to provide for better \npassenger safety by creat ing maintenance corridor blocks, minimizing \nconflicts in existing time table, generation of additional paths for \nfreight traffic and speeding up train services. Since, November -2021, \ntrain services are being operated with rationalised time table and all \nMail/Express trains are being operated with regular numbers, subject to \noperational feasibility.   \n Owing to operational reasons, 12831/12832 Dhanbad -Bhuvaneswar \nGarib Rath Express (Khurda Road Division of East Coast Railway), \n15071/15072 Lucknow -Mau Jn Expr ess (Lucknow Junction Division of \nNorth Eastern Railway) and 12847/12848 Howrah -Digha Express \n(Kharagpur Division of South Eastern Railway)  are the Mail/Express \ntrains which have not been restored yet.   \n Linen/Bedrolls have been restored in all eligible running trains post \nCovid except train No. 12740/12739  Secunderabad-Visakhapatnam \nGarib Rath Express. Catering services in trains have resumed from the \nrespective date of resumption of train services after the Covid -19 \npandemic. These services are provided  through Pantry Cars /Mini \nPantries, Train Side Vending and Static Units at en -route stations. In \naddition, passengers travelling in the trains have the facility to order \nfood of their choice through e-Catering services. \n***** ",
